  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Crisis Risk Network is designed to help countries and communities navigate an increasingly uncertain global environment marked by economic shocks, political instability, climate change, and rapid technological change. The initiative, led by UNDP in partnership with governments, UN agencies, and technical experts, aims to safeguard development gains and reduce reliance on humanitarian assistance by integrating risk awareness and resilience into all aspects of planning and programming. Central</narrative>
